      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've definitely been wanting to see a more performant cloth component. Even for a tiny piece of cloth I find the vertex limit is too low to be able to get a good result, and even cloth that's twice the vertex density still has issues.\n\nI've heard good things about magicka and would buy it if I could, if the limits were more generous. I don't know how it performs, but would be quite happy - ecstatic even - with a VRC Cloth, since clearly there is at least one person on the team who knows their stuff since Physbones and VRC Constraints are both so much better than the existing versions.\n\nI do feel like this is something that should be prioritized, because there is a real need. If we had a performant version that worked well it'd get more use.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
